<title>RUSSIA: Russia gets $42 mln loan from U.S. Ex-Im Bank.</title>
<headline>Russia gets $42 mln loan from U.S. Ex-Im Bank.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government has decided to take a $42 million credit from the U.S. Ex-Im Bank to fund housing construction, a government spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The decision, taken last week, channels the funds into several areas, including Ulyanovsk, Moscow and Tomsk regions, he told a news conference.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
